  "id": "Compound::DB01213 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Fomepizole is implicated in the fatty acid omega-oxidation pathway through its interaction with Adh1c and Adh1b, which are enzymes involved in the metabolic processing of fatty acids. This pathway is ultimately linked to Cyp2e1, an enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates, including fatty acids and xenobiotics. The evidence suggests that Fomepizole may influence Cyp2e1 through its role in modulating the fatty acid oxidation process, potentially by affecting the availability of substrates or by altering the activity of the enzymes involved. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Fomepizole could impact Cyp2e1, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
